---
// The privacy page (scope row 18, spec 0007), in the shared site frame (spec 0009). Its words are plain and factual; the contact
// address comes from the consent text through PRIVACY_CONTACT (src/lib/frame.ts reads convex/consentText.ts), so the page, the
// footer and the notice a student agrees to cannot differ. Update the words whenever the consent text or a service that handles
// student data changes.
import Frame from "../../layouts/Frame.astro";
import { HOME_PATH, PRIVACY_CONTACT } from "../../lib/frame";

const contact = PRIVACY_CONTACT;
---
<Frame
  title="Privacy"
  description="What DhiRise keeps about you, why, who helps us look after it, and how to reach us."
  back={{ href: HOME_PATH, label: "← Back" }}
>
  <article class="fr-card fr-prose">
    <h1>Privacy at DhiRise</h1>
    <p class="fr-lead">The short version: we ask only for what we need to give you your study picture, we keep it private, we do not sell it, and you can ask us to fix it or erase it at any time.</p>

    <section>
      <h2>1. What we keep</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name, age and class.</li>
        <li>The email of the Google account you use to sign in.</li>
        <li>Your answers to the 18 questions, and the result and report we prepare from them.</li>
        <li>A PDF copy of your report, so you can download it later.</li>
        <li>One small copy of the profile picture from your Google account, and nothing else from your Google profile (see section 5).</li>
        <li>Your mobile number, only if you add it, and whether you asked to join the Dhi early access group on WhatsApp.</li>
        <li>The feedback you write, if you write any.</li>
        <li>A private link to your report, if you tap Share: its end date, and that you agreed to the sharing notice.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. Why we keep it</h2>
      <p>To make your study profile, save your check, show you your result and report, and message you about your result and the Dhi app. Your answers are also used to improve this check.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. Who helps us look after it</h2>
      <p>We use a few services to run DhiRise. Each one handles only what it needs to do its job.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Google</b> lets you sign in. We get your name, email and profile picture from it. A copy of the mobile number step and of your feedback also goes to a Google Sheet kept by the DhiRise team.</li>
        <li><b>Convex</b> is our database. Your profile, answers, result and PDF copy are stored there.</li>
        <li><b>Cloudflare</b> serves this website. Its service called <b>Cloudflare Browser Run</b> opens our own report page and prints it to a PDF, so your report data passes through Cloudflare when your PDF copy is made.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell your data.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. Your report and your PDF copy</h2>
      <p>You can open your report and download your PDF copy. Named members of the DhiRise team can also open your report to help you. Each time one does, we record who opened it and when.</p>
      <p>Some answers can show how you feel, for example when you feel low. That is shown only to you, in your own report. It is not in the PDF copy, not in the team's Google Sheet and not on any leaderboard.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5. Your Google profile picture</h2>
      <p>DhiRise saves one small copy of the profile picture from your Google account, and nothing else from your Google profile. We show it next to your name, so DhiRise feels like yours. There is no separate question about it. It is on for every student. If you joined before the picture was added, the words you agreed to when you began did not mention it, so this page is where we tell you. You can take it off whenever you like, as described below.</p>
      <p>Your picture can be seen by:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>You, on your own screens and in your report.</li>
        <li>Other students, if the leaderboard shows pictures.</li>
        <li>Anyone you give a report link to.</li>
        <li>Named members of the DhiRise team.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>You can remove it at any time. Open your report and tap <b>Remove my picture</b>. We delete our copy, and your initial shows instead. You can bring it back with <b>Use my Google picture</b>.</p>
      <p>A removed picture can stay in browser copies for up to an hour. PDF copies of your report and report links that were already made may keep the picture they drew. Asking us to erase your data removes those too. A PDF copy made very early, before your picture was saved, may have no picture at all.</p>
      <p>If a picture is not right for DhiRise, the team can also take it off. To ask, write to <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>6. Your report link</h2>
      <p>When you tap Share, DhiRise can make a private link to your report. Before the first link we show you a short notice and ask you to agree. If you are under 18, you also tick that you have checked with a parent or guardian.</p>
      <p>Anyone who has the link can read your whole report. They see your first name and your profile picture, and they can copy the link and pass it on. They cannot see your age, class, email, phone number or your private notes. The page sets no cookies and loads nothing from other websites.</p>
      <p>The link ends by itself 90 days after the last time you tapped Share, and never later than one year after it was made. You can turn it off at any time with <b>Stop sharing</b>, under the share buttons on your report. After that, the old link only says that it is off or has ended. A named member of the DhiRise team can also turn a link off after a complaint.</p>
      <p>The link is part of the page address, so it can stay in a browser's history and in the chat where you send it. Share it only with people you trust. Asking us to erase your data removes your link too. To ask, write to <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>7. If you are under 18</h2>
      <p>A parent or guardian must be with you and must agree before you use DhiRise. Please do not continue alone.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>8. Your choices</h2>
      <p>You may take back your consent, correct your details, or ask us to erase them, which includes your PDF copy. Write to <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>. Taking back your consent does not change a result that was already prepared.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>9. Who to contact</h2>
      <p>For any question or complaint about your data, write to the DhiRise privacy contact at <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>. This is the same address as in the notice you agree to before you begin.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>10. Changes</h2>
      <p>If this page or the notice changes, new students see the new notice when they sign up. We keep the exact words of every notice a student agreed to.</p>
      <p>Last updated: 11 October 2026.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Frame>
